254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (The project was inspired by the film Playtime. I wanted to design the game's progression around existing tools, using puzzles and music as the driving mechanics. My criterion for selecting ideas was whether they were interesting and distinctive enough to convey the game's particular atmosphere and emotional tone. The concept went through one major pivot before taking its final form: I originally intended to trace the history of video games, or the history of the medium itself, through the level progression. This proved too complex, so I abandoned it in favor of a more focused, puzzle-and-music-driven experience.)
/E (The project was inspired by the film Playtime. I wanted to design the game's progression around existing tools, using puzzles and music as the driving mechanics. My criterion for selecting ideas was whether they were interesting and distinctive enough to convey the game's particular atmosphere and emotional tone. The concept went through one major pivot before taking its final form: I originally intended to trace the history of video games, or the history of the medium itself, through the level progression. This proved too complex, so I abandoned it in favor of a more focused, puzzle-and-music-driven experience.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
