275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 109 0 R
/T (My iterative process can be summarized in three stages: the conceptual stage, where I gathered reference images, mood boards, and music; the production stage, where I built a basic white box for the level and then expanded its space and structure on top of the puzzle logic; and the refinement stage, where I designed specific puzzles and paired them with sound design. One playtest revealed that players found the puzzles too difficult to solve, so I lowered the difficulty and made object interactions more intuitive. In balancing personal expression against player readability, I consistently prioritized readability and a smooth path to completion first, treating environmental design and atmosphere-building as secondary considerations.)
/E (My iterative process can be summarized in three stages: the conceptual stage, where I gathered reference images, mood boards, and music; the production stage, where I built a basic white box for the level and then expanded its space and structure on top of the puzzle logic; and the refinement stage, where I designed specific puzzles and paired them with sound design. One playtest revealed that players found the puzzles too difficult to solve, so I lowered the difficulty and made object interactions more intuitive. In balancing personal expression against player readability, I consistently prioritized readability and a smooth path to completion first, treating environmental design and atmosphere-building as secondary considerations.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
