/Title (The stage most prone to delay in my timeline was the conceptual phase, where I sometimes abandoned promising ideas too early. For instance, platforming initially seemed like a dated mechanic, but once I developed it further, I found that the materials and arrangement of the platforms could significantly increase the sense of fun. A concrete example of resolving the tension between perfectionism and deadlines was cutting a planned chase sequence from the level, since it would have disrupted the player's exploratory rhythm and clashed with the game's overall tone.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1681 0 R
/First 1712 0 R
/Last 1713 0 R
/Count -2
